1
00:00:20,491 --> 00:00:22,581
JANUARY 1014 AD - OUTSKIRTS
OF GAINSBOROUGH, NORTHEAST ENGLAND

2
00:00:22,661 --> 00:00:24,421
Thorkell's using it as an excuse.

3
00:00:24,791 --> 00:00:26,831
That's the only reason I can think of.

4
00:00:26,921 --> 00:00:28,381
But, Floki,

5
00:00:28,841 --> 00:00:31,341
-the reports from Derby--
-The left flank is undermanned!

6
00:00:31,421 --> 00:00:33,301
Don't underestimate a force of 500 soldiers.

7
00:00:33,381 --> 00:00:35,011
We're talking about Thorkell's army!

8
00:00:35,511 --> 00:00:36,511
Floki.

9
00:00:36,591 --> 00:00:38,141
If the reports are true,

10
00:00:38,221 --> 00:00:40,261
then your actions will be disrespectful.

11
00:00:40,351 --> 00:00:41,721
It's impossible.

12
00:00:41,811 --> 00:00:46,101
His Highness Canute can't be alive
and with Thorkell as one of his followers.

13
00:00:47,231 --> 00:00:49,021
It's impossible!

14
00:00:57,491 --> 00:01:01,581
Hey, Floki! Want to fight? I'll fight you.

15
00:01:01,661 --> 00:01:03,371
Restrain yourself, Thorkell.

16
00:01:04,541 --> 00:01:06,671
I thought I sent a messenger several days ago

17
00:01:06,751 --> 00:01:09,711
to notify you of my return, Floki.

18
00:01:10,591 --> 00:01:13,711
Do you always greet your guests
with spears in hand?

19
00:01:13,801 --> 00:01:17,341
No, of course not...

20
00:01:18,801 --> 00:01:22,221
Askeladd! Why are you here?

21
00:01:22,311 --> 00:01:24,521
Are you deaf?

22
00:01:26,231 --> 00:01:29,231
I'm asking you whether you're going

23
00:01:29,311 --> 00:01:32,321
to draw your bows against a member
of the royal family of Denmark.

24
00:01:32,401 --> 00:01:34,031
No...

25
00:01:35,151 --> 00:01:38,031
We Jomsvikings received an inaccurate report

26
00:01:38,111 --> 00:01:41,741
that an enemy army was going to attack...

27
00:01:45,201 --> 00:01:47,411
I apologize.

28
00:01:49,041 --> 00:01:51,211
Notify the king

29
00:01:51,291 --> 00:01:53,801
that I shall be at his hall by evening.

30
00:01:53,881 --> 00:01:55,261
Make sure you report accurately.

31
00:02:07,351 --> 00:02:09,191
What in the world happened?

32
00:02:10,561 --> 00:02:12,821
He's a completely different person.

33
00:03:45,031 --> 00:03:47,951
GAINSBOROUGH CASTLE TOWN
DANISH ARMY HEADQUARTERS

34
00:03:48,791 --> 00:03:51,161
Everyone, listen to me while we walk.

35
00:03:52,251 --> 00:03:54,001
We must not strike yet.

36
00:03:54,081 --> 00:03:55,081
CROWN

37
00:03:55,171 --> 00:03:57,501
I don't have many allies within this army.

38
00:03:58,461 --> 00:04:01,131
If we strike now, they'll label us as traitors.

39
00:04:01,221 --> 00:04:02,841
We need time to prepare.

40
00:04:03,841 --> 00:04:07,101
Thorkell. You betrayed them once,

41
00:04:07,181 --> 00:04:09,561
but you're still popular among the warriors.

42
00:04:09,641 --> 00:04:11,851
Spend time with the leaders
of all the clans

43
00:04:11,931 --> 00:04:13,891
and mend ties with them.

44
00:04:14,231 --> 00:04:16,061
In other words, are you telling me

45
00:04:16,151 --> 00:04:19,611
to go drink as much as I want,
and that you'll pay for it?

46
00:04:19,691 --> 00:04:22,151
As long as you invite the other leaders.
Now, go.

47
00:04:22,241 --> 00:04:25,031
What a wonderful order!

48
00:04:25,491 --> 00:04:28,531
I'm so glad I decided to follow you.

49
00:04:28,621 --> 00:04:30,291
-Let's go!
-Hey!

50
00:04:31,831 --> 00:04:34,461
Askeladd. Come with me to see the king.

51
00:04:34,541 --> 00:04:36,541
I want to hear what you think of him.

52
00:04:36,631 --> 00:04:37,501
Understood.

53
00:04:38,091 --> 00:04:40,251
And about the future.

54
00:04:40,341 --> 00:04:41,881
How will we achieve it?

55
00:04:41,961 --> 00:04:43,421
Understood.

56
00:04:43,511 --> 00:04:46,141
I think an assassination would be best
in the short run.

57
00:04:48,011 --> 00:04:50,311
Your brother, His Highness Harald,

58
00:04:50,391 --> 00:04:53,561
is far away in Denmark right now.
This is a good opportunity.

59
00:04:54,061 --> 00:04:56,441
If the king passes away right now,

60
00:04:56,521 --> 00:04:58,861
then command of the army in England

61
00:04:58,941 --> 00:05:00,731
is going to pass to you.

62
00:05:01,821 --> 00:05:05,991
However, if we do so, we must hide
the person responsible for it.

63
00:05:10,161 --> 00:05:11,371
Thorfinn.

64
00:05:11,451 --> 00:05:15,001
In the future, I'll assign you with other tasks
in addition to being a guard.

65
00:05:15,081 --> 00:05:16,121
I'm counting on you.

66
00:05:16,211 --> 00:05:17,961
Don't give me orders.

67
00:05:18,041 --> 00:05:20,631
I never said I decided to work for you.

68
00:05:22,211 --> 00:05:24,381
Please forgive him for his impertinence.

69
00:05:24,471 --> 00:05:27,591
I'll make sure I instruct this idiot properly.

70
00:05:33,221 --> 00:05:34,271
God...

71
00:05:35,271 --> 00:05:39,401
must be watching us, even as we stand here now.

72
00:05:41,481 --> 00:05:43,401
People losing friends,

73
00:05:43,481 --> 00:05:46,241
and parents and children killing each other...

74
00:05:46,321 --> 00:05:48,821
He must be looking down on everything

75
00:05:48,911 --> 00:05:52,201
from up high in heaven.

76
00:05:55,831 --> 00:05:57,081
I'll never forgive him.

77
00:06:00,001 --> 00:06:03,421
I'm going to create paradise on earth.

78
00:06:03,501 --> 00:06:05,921
A peaceful and prosperous place.

79
00:06:06,011 --> 00:06:09,091
A utopia for those who go through
suffering in their lives.

80
00:06:10,761 --> 00:06:13,721
I may not be able to achieve it in one generation,

81
00:06:13,811 --> 00:06:15,681
but I'm still going to take

82
00:06:15,771 --> 00:06:17,311
the first step.

83
00:06:18,891 --> 00:06:21,061
I'm sure that God will cherish me

84
00:06:21,151 --> 00:06:23,691
and summon me to his side.

85
00:06:23,771 --> 00:06:25,441
But...

86
00:06:25,531 --> 00:06:27,861
in that moment I will tell him:

87
00:06:29,201 --> 00:06:32,491
"We don't need heaven, nor its trials, any longer.

88
00:06:32,571 --> 00:06:36,041
Our paradise is on earth."

89
00:06:40,041 --> 00:06:42,541
We're going to take back what we lost.

90
00:06:43,541 --> 00:06:46,591
I'm willing to turn into a demon
if that's what it takes to do it.

91
00:06:49,421 --> 00:06:50,971
I will help you,

92
00:06:52,221 --> 00:06:53,391
Your Highness.

93
00:07:08,781 --> 00:07:10,611
Welcome back.

94
00:07:11,821 --> 00:07:14,531
I'm glad, Canute.

95
00:07:15,831 --> 00:07:18,001
Thank you for your kind words.

96
00:07:18,081 --> 00:07:21,331
I lost the soldiers you had entrusted to me.

97
00:07:21,421 --> 00:07:23,131
Your words are more than I deserve.

98
00:07:24,421 --> 00:07:26,131
Come closer.

99
00:07:28,631 --> 00:07:29,971
Wait.

100
00:07:31,511 --> 00:07:33,011
What do you think, Thorfinn?

101
00:07:33,181 --> 00:07:34,801
Yeah, they're there.

102
00:07:35,261 --> 00:07:37,101
About 20 of them.

103
00:07:37,181 --> 00:07:39,771
There are some up high too. Archers.

104
00:07:40,811 --> 00:07:43,271
Your Highness. It's an ambush.

105
00:07:43,691 --> 00:07:45,311
It seems that the king

106
00:07:45,901 --> 00:07:48,571
knows about our intentions.

107
00:07:50,111 --> 00:07:53,781
What's wrong? Without further delay, come closer.

108
00:07:55,531 --> 00:07:57,201
You two.

109
00:07:57,281 --> 00:07:59,411
You must not draw your swords, no matter what.

110
00:08:00,411 --> 00:08:02,211
He who draws his sword first loses.

111
00:08:03,461 --> 00:08:06,381
That's the type of fight this is.

112
00:08:20,021 --> 00:08:22,231
My eyes have gotten used to the darkness.

113
00:08:22,941 --> 00:08:24,901
If I get a little closer,

114
00:08:24,981 --> 00:08:26,771
I'll be able to see the king's face.

115
00:08:27,771 --> 00:08:30,031
If I can see his face...

116
00:08:30,111 --> 00:08:31,361
Stop.

117
00:08:35,031 --> 00:08:38,661
Right there is fine. Kneel down.

118
00:08:45,121 --> 00:08:47,421
His eyes are tired.

119
00:08:47,501 --> 00:08:49,171
Is this who

120
00:08:49,251 --> 00:08:51,171
the king of the Danes is?

121
00:08:51,261 --> 00:08:52,421
Askeladd.

122
00:08:59,351 --> 00:09:03,431
What happened to Ragnar? I don't see him.

123
00:09:04,351 --> 00:09:06,851
He died. In Mercia.

124
00:09:07,851 --> 00:09:11,191
I see. That's too bad.

125
00:09:12,191 --> 00:09:14,781
He was a loyal subject.

126
00:09:18,451 --> 00:09:23,001
In normal circumstances, we should be
celebrating your return with food and drink.

127
00:09:24,411 --> 00:09:26,711
However,

128
00:09:26,791 --> 00:09:30,791
I wanted to speak with you once informally.

129
00:09:33,011 --> 00:09:34,881
Canute. Only you. Rise.

130
00:09:36,631 --> 00:09:38,681
Walk ten steps forward.

131
00:09:54,781 --> 00:09:57,571
You face has changed

132
00:09:57,651 --> 00:10:00,571
in just a short time.

133
00:10:00,661 --> 00:10:03,331
You look like me when I was young.

134
00:10:03,991 --> 00:10:05,411
Then

135
00:10:05,501 --> 00:10:08,711
you must understand what's in my heart.

136
00:10:10,381 --> 00:10:12,591
You're a troublesome child.

137
00:10:12,671 --> 00:10:14,801
I never imagined you'd become

138
00:10:14,881 --> 00:10:16,471
just like me, even in that regard.

139
00:10:17,761 --> 00:10:18,931
Children

140
00:10:19,011 --> 00:10:23,141
grow up watching what their parents do.

141
00:10:23,221 --> 00:10:24,851
Do not blame yourself.

142
00:10:26,931 --> 00:10:28,851
Long ago, when I was young,

143
00:10:29,941 --> 00:10:33,981
I drove my father, the former king, out of this country

144
00:10:34,651 --> 00:10:37,321
and seized this crown.

145
00:10:37,401 --> 00:10:41,741
I did it because I believed it was the best
thing to do for the kingdom.

146
00:10:42,951 --> 00:10:47,621
The former king was cruel, but he was also a coward.

147
00:10:48,621 --> 00:10:53,631
The world would sink into chaos if someone
like him had the crown.

148
00:10:54,711 --> 00:10:57,761
How can he say that when he's surrounded
by this many guards?

149
00:10:57,841 --> 00:10:59,841
Shut up. He'll hear you.

150
00:11:01,091 --> 00:11:04,511
So, you decided not to keep up the pretense,
Your Highness?

151
00:11:05,181 --> 00:11:08,681
Don't forget you're surrounded by the enemy.

152
00:11:09,981 --> 00:11:12,231
I thought that I had done something great,

153
00:11:12,311 --> 00:11:15,401
and that I could do great things.

154
00:11:15,861 --> 00:11:18,531
Until I put this on, that is.

155
00:11:21,031 --> 00:11:23,201
This crown

156
00:11:23,281 --> 00:11:25,991
has its own will.

157
00:11:28,331 --> 00:11:30,291
Once you wear this crown, you can command

158
00:11:30,371 --> 00:11:33,041
a thousand ships and 10,000 men.

159
00:11:33,131 --> 00:11:37,251
You can take all kinds of treasure from distant lands.

160
00:11:39,131 --> 00:11:42,841
A power like that of the gods
is bestowed upon you.

161
00:11:45,301 --> 00:11:46,141
However...

162
00:11:48,641 --> 00:11:51,061
However, Canute,

163
00:11:51,141 --> 00:11:54,021
the king isn't the one who uses that power.

164
00:11:55,021 --> 00:11:57,981
That power is used by the will of the crown.

165
00:12:01,741 --> 00:12:03,321
Do you mean

166
00:12:03,411 --> 00:12:05,201
the crown ordered you...

167
00:12:06,201 --> 00:12:07,991
to kill me?

168
00:12:10,291 --> 00:12:14,621
There are only two things that the crown
orders the king to do.

169
00:12:14,711 --> 00:12:16,671
It orders him to use his power,

170
00:12:16,751 --> 00:12:19,091
and to increase his power.

171
00:12:19,171 --> 00:12:21,511
Resistance is futile.

172
00:12:22,671 --> 00:12:26,471
The crown does not want you.

173
00:12:48,201 --> 00:12:50,041
Canute.

174
00:12:50,331 --> 00:12:53,001
I'll give you part of Cornwall.

175
00:12:53,871 --> 00:12:56,121
Live your days in peace there

176
00:12:56,211 --> 00:12:58,631
while reading the Bible.

177
00:12:59,461 --> 00:13:03,801
If you refuse, then you'll die here.

178
00:13:06,221 --> 00:13:10,221
Did the crown make you say that too,

179
00:13:10,311 --> 00:13:12,601
-Your Highness?
-Your Highness!

180
00:13:12,681 --> 00:13:15,441
I humbly ask you to let me speak.

181
00:13:19,021 --> 00:13:20,021
State your name.

182
00:13:21,361 --> 00:13:23,241
I'm Canute's follower,

183
00:13:23,691 --> 00:13:26,031
Askeladd, son of Olaf.

184
00:13:26,701 --> 00:13:31,411
With all due respect, consider whether your actions
are in line with the will of the crown.

185
00:13:34,161 --> 00:13:35,501
Continue.

186
00:13:37,121 --> 00:13:38,711
His Highness Canute

187
00:13:38,791 --> 00:13:42,501
stole Thorkell and the military power he commands
away from London.

188
00:13:42,961 --> 00:13:45,971
If you become the king of England,

189
00:13:46,051 --> 00:13:49,551
then London will have no choice but to surrender.

190
00:13:50,601 --> 00:13:54,561
The wealth of London will become yours untouched,
Your Highness.

191
00:13:55,351 --> 00:13:57,191
His Highness Canute

192
00:13:57,271 --> 00:13:59,271
is the one who made the sacrifice

193
00:13:59,351 --> 00:14:01,191
for this great achievement.

194
00:14:02,521 --> 00:14:06,241
Is it not unreasonable to punish the man who rendered
such distinguished service?

195
00:14:06,321 --> 00:14:07,821
Your handling of this matter

196
00:14:07,901 --> 00:14:09,951
would deeply trouble

197
00:14:10,031 --> 00:14:12,951
your generals when the time comes
to divide the new territory.

198
00:14:13,031 --> 00:14:15,201
Please reconsider this matter.

199
00:14:19,331 --> 00:14:21,421
You're a man who's good with words.

200
00:14:22,631 --> 00:14:25,881
Askeladd. "The one covered in ashes"?

201
00:14:28,171 --> 00:14:30,801
That's your nickname.

202
00:14:30,891 --> 00:14:33,761
Tell me the name that your father gave you.

203
00:14:35,681 --> 00:14:38,181
I'm only known as Askeladd.

204
00:14:38,271 --> 00:14:41,231
My father didn't give me a name.

205
00:14:43,901 --> 00:14:47,241
You must be the child of one of his mistresses. No...

206
00:14:47,321 --> 00:14:50,071
You must be a child he forced one of his slaves to have.

207
00:15:01,171 --> 00:15:05,381
What's going on?
I've never seen Askeladd get so mad.

208
00:15:06,591 --> 00:15:08,471
Canute.

209
00:15:08,551 --> 00:15:11,261
You have a good follower.

210
00:15:11,761 --> 00:15:13,891
It is just as he said.

211
00:15:14,431 --> 00:15:17,891
I have to reward you.

212
00:15:19,061 --> 00:15:21,521
I am leaving for York tomorrow.

213
00:15:21,601 --> 00:15:24,061
There, I shall throw a banquet.

214
00:15:25,071 --> 00:15:27,231
I shall give you your reward there.

215
00:15:47,001 --> 00:15:49,591
My blood froze just now, Your Highness.

216
00:15:50,631 --> 00:15:53,131
What are you so worried about?

217
00:15:53,221 --> 00:15:56,601
As you already know, the king

218
00:15:56,681 --> 00:16:00,101
doesn't have enough justification to kill me right now.

219
00:16:00,181 --> 00:16:02,441
He's the man who they call the wise king.

220
00:16:03,351 --> 00:16:05,361
As long as we don't do anything reckless,

221
00:16:05,441 --> 00:16:08,321
it's safer to lie within the king's bosom.

222
00:16:09,111 --> 00:16:13,451
Then that's all the more reason to refrain from
provoking him like you did just now.

223
00:16:16,451 --> 00:16:18,331
It's nothing of consequence.

224
00:16:18,661 --> 00:16:21,541
King Sweyn is a slave to the crown.

225
00:16:24,211 --> 00:16:26,541
The power of the crown.

226
00:16:26,631 --> 00:16:29,251
I will show him how to use it.

227
00:16:31,011 --> 00:16:32,721
Askeladd...

228
00:16:36,011 --> 00:16:39,391
I must be wary of him.

229
00:16:42,771 --> 00:16:44,811
Cheers!

230
00:16:44,891 --> 00:16:47,561
All right! Don't be shy!

231
00:16:47,651 --> 00:16:50,361
This is all on His Highness Canute!

232
00:16:51,651 --> 00:16:54,321
Long live the prince!

233
00:17:00,161 --> 00:17:03,201
-That's his 57th glass!
-He's a monster!

234
00:17:03,871 --> 00:17:07,961
Hey! You've been drinking a lot. Who are you?

235
00:17:08,421 --> 00:17:11,001
I don't remember inviting you here.

236
00:17:11,091 --> 00:17:14,341
I'm Willibald. Did you forget me?

237
00:17:14,421 --> 00:17:15,261
What?

238
00:17:17,471 --> 00:17:18,551
What?

239
00:17:19,051 --> 00:17:21,471
-Your beard is gone!
-You look so young. How old are you?

240
00:17:21,561 --> 00:17:22,601
I'm 23.

241
00:17:22,681 --> 00:17:25,021
-No way!
-You're in your early 20s?

242
00:17:25,101 --> 00:17:27,691
All right! It's my turn next!

243
00:17:27,771 --> 00:17:29,191
The captain is up now!

244
00:17:29,271 --> 00:17:31,981
You're behind by 58 glasses!

245
00:17:32,071 --> 00:17:33,651
What a strange man.

246
00:17:34,071 --> 00:17:37,321
He does whatever he wants,
but no one hates him.

247
00:17:38,361 --> 00:17:39,241
True.

248
00:17:41,581 --> 00:17:43,291
So? What do you think?

249
00:17:44,291 --> 00:17:46,831
Do you think you can kill him? The king?

250
00:17:49,041 --> 00:17:50,921
It's going to be difficult.

251
00:17:51,001 --> 00:17:53,301
That's what I'd say.

252
00:17:55,091 --> 00:17:58,131
I got the impression he's a smart man.

253
00:17:58,341 --> 00:18:02,431
He's discerning, and he's a man of action
who can make the first move.

254
00:18:03,431 --> 00:18:08,351
When he saw that we wouldn't buckle under his threats,
he switched to a different strategy.

255
00:18:08,441 --> 00:18:10,941
I would say he's skilled in war.

256
00:18:11,941 --> 00:18:16,151
No wonder he's the king of the country.

257
00:18:16,241 --> 00:18:17,741
He's a tough opponent.

258
00:18:19,071 --> 00:18:23,331
Even if we're planning to kill him someday,
I guess now's not the time.

259
00:18:23,411 --> 00:18:27,041
Let's submit to his wishes for the time being

260
00:18:27,121 --> 00:18:29,211
while we wait for our chance.

261
00:18:30,381 --> 00:18:32,591
Your Highness! Your Highness!

262
00:18:34,841 --> 00:18:38,011
I'm so glad you returned safely!

263
00:18:38,091 --> 00:18:41,591
Do you have any idea how much I, Gunnar,
worried about you?

264
00:18:41,681 --> 00:18:44,851
I apologize that I was unable to greet you at the castle.

265
00:18:44,931 --> 00:18:48,521
I just returned from a foreign country.

266
00:18:48,601 --> 00:18:52,271
I always believed you'd return, of course!

267
00:18:52,361 --> 00:18:55,611
Oh, is this gentleman over here your new follower?

268
00:18:55,691 --> 00:18:58,151
Can you introduce me?

269
00:18:58,241 --> 00:19:01,741
This is Ragnar's brother, Gunnar.
Please become acquainted with each other.

270
00:19:02,821 --> 00:19:05,991
I'm Askeladd, son of Olaf.

271
00:19:06,081 --> 00:19:09,411
Oh, you look like a dependable character.

272
00:19:09,501 --> 00:19:11,621
I'm Gunnar.

273
00:19:11,711 --> 00:19:13,081
By the way, Your Highness...

274
00:19:14,541 --> 00:19:17,801
that plan from a long time ago...
The prospects look brighter now.

275
00:19:17,881 --> 00:19:19,921
I'm talking about the Duchy of Normandy.

276
00:19:20,011 --> 00:19:23,261
I wanted to talk to you about it later
with my brother.

277
00:19:24,261 --> 00:19:26,351
Ragnar is dead.

278
00:19:26,431 --> 00:19:28,641
Sorry for making you go through all that trouble.

279
00:19:29,641 --> 00:19:32,101
And I'm not going to go into exile.

280
00:19:32,401 --> 00:19:34,231
-Your Highness? What did you say?
-I'm sorry

281
00:19:34,311 --> 00:19:37,191
to put you to the trouble of
running around to the other countries.

282
00:19:37,821 --> 00:19:40,651
I just picked a fight with King Sweyn.

283
00:19:40,741 --> 00:19:43,241
-Please help me.
-My brother...

284
00:19:43,321 --> 00:19:44,161
Gunnar.

285
00:19:46,121 --> 00:19:49,871
Your job is to keep an eye on the king
and report back to me.

286
00:19:49,951 --> 00:19:52,581
Choose soldiers who you trust.

287
00:19:52,921 --> 00:19:56,791
Your Highness! You must not talk about that
in a place like this!

288
00:19:56,881 --> 00:20:00,091
I don't care. This is actually a good place
to talk in secret.

289
00:20:00,421 --> 00:20:01,801
Your Highness...

290
00:20:03,091 --> 00:20:04,891
You've changed.

291
00:20:09,221 --> 00:20:13,061
Of course I've changed.
I must change everything.

292
00:20:24,491 --> 00:20:26,991
Gunnar's no good.

293
00:20:27,331 --> 00:20:30,501
I don't think he's as loyal to the prince
as he says.

294
00:20:43,341 --> 00:20:46,471
How wonderful that you're so devoted
to staying prepared.

295
00:20:46,551 --> 00:20:49,061
Doesn't your right arm hurt?

296
00:20:49,141 --> 00:20:50,721
-Askeladd.
-What?

297
00:20:55,481 --> 00:20:58,231
I see. You're going home?

298
00:20:59,321 --> 00:21:01,861
I know you said you don't care,

299
00:21:01,941 --> 00:21:04,361
but we did betray you.

300
00:21:04,901 --> 00:21:08,491
I don't know how I can face you anymore--
Ouch!

301
00:21:09,871 --> 00:21:11,291
I got you!

302
00:21:11,371 --> 00:21:15,621
And look what happened to my brother.

303
00:21:15,711 --> 00:21:18,331
I hope Bjorn's wounds heal.

304
00:21:19,841 --> 00:21:23,631
Atli! And you still call yourself a Viking?

305
00:21:23,721 --> 00:21:27,681
I can't believe I had such an honest man working for me.

306
00:21:30,761 --> 00:21:33,271
Bjorn's not going to last long.

307
00:21:33,351 --> 00:21:35,391
The wound reached his intestines.

308
00:21:37,441 --> 00:21:38,691
Now,

309
00:21:38,771 --> 00:21:42,731
Thorfinn is the only one left from among my men.

310
00:21:42,821 --> 00:21:44,991
It's the perfect time for making a fresh start.

311
00:21:47,161 --> 00:21:48,451
A bracelet?

312
00:21:48,531 --> 00:21:50,071
It's gold. Take it.

313
00:21:50,241 --> 00:21:53,161
What? I don't need it! There's no reason for me to take it.

314
00:21:53,241 --> 00:21:55,041
Just take it.

315
00:21:55,121 --> 00:21:57,751
There's no such thing as having too much money
while traveling.

316
00:22:00,591 --> 00:22:05,051
Sorry. I appreciate it.

317
00:22:05,131 --> 00:22:05,971
What?

318
00:22:06,051 --> 00:22:09,641
Hey! Are you going to give it to me or not?

319
00:22:09,721 --> 00:22:10,971
I have one condition.

320
00:22:12,891 --> 00:22:15,101
Never pick up a sword ever again.

321
00:22:15,181 --> 00:22:17,481
Swords don't suit you, Atli.

322
00:22:17,811 --> 00:22:20,191
Raise some sheep, get a wife,

323
00:22:20,271 --> 00:22:22,481
have a kid, and die in your bed.

324
00:22:23,521 --> 00:22:27,201
If I see you on the battlefield in the future,
I'm going to kill you,

325
00:22:27,281 --> 00:22:28,741
even if you're on my side.

326
00:22:30,241 --> 00:22:32,991
Okay. I understand.

327
00:22:43,001 --> 00:22:45,551
-What's that?
-This?

328
00:22:45,631 --> 00:22:47,631
It's something important.

329
00:22:47,721 --> 00:22:49,011
It's pretty.

330
00:22:57,851 --> 00:22:59,641
That's too expensive! Give me a discount.

331
00:22:59,731 --> 00:23:01,311
Show me some younger women!

332
00:23:01,401 --> 00:23:03,231
-Bring the younger women!
-Any takers?

333
00:23:03,311 --> 00:23:05,481
FEBRUARY 1014 AD - YORK, DANISH
ARMY-OCCUPIED TOWN, NORTHUMBRIA REGION
